1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
STOP! Built your team with ONLY favorites? You might be losing Judocoins… and not even know it. Here's why!

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Team's ready… now what? Here, you play two scoreboards.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Points move you up the ranking. Judocoins decide the team you can afford next round.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Every athlete's price is a points target. Score more than he costs? He rises. Score less? He drops.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:44,000
But here's where it HURTS. Look at this favorite: he cost eighteen. Won one fight by ippon… lost the next by waza-ari. Eight points. He dropped to thirteen… and YOU lost five Judocoins.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Now a bargain at six who scored sixteen. He rose to eleven, and you gained two and a half.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Now the rule that changes EVERYTHING: when an athlete rises, you keep HALF. When he drops… you take the WHOLE drop.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Favorites rise too, if they score more than they cost: an eighteen who scores twenty-four goes to twenty-one.

9
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,000
And your captain doubles the points… not the Judocoins.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:26,000
So don't just ask who'll win. Ask who'll score MORE than he costs! Send this to a friend who picked only favorites… and build your team on Ippon League.
